Id: krb003w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_kerberos
References: krb5.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 3.3, 5.2; NIST AC-3, IA-5(7); ISO 5.17, 8.3; CE User access control

A Kerberos keytab is readable by anyone. It holds the service's
long-term keys, so whoever copies it becomes the service. Leave it
readable by root alone.
